## Pipeline / persistence
- Error-path `record_sync_run` in FULL build — `orchestrator/full_build.py` has no try/except around the pipeline; parse / C5 / DB failures propagate uncaught and never land an audit row with `status=ERROR`. Wrap `_full_build` the same way `patch_build.py` already does (lines 127–142 there are the model)
- Open a RUNNING `sync_runs` row at dispatch start — `orchestrator/utils/db_utils.py:record_sync_run` is an end-of-pipeline insert only; `WS /repos/{graph_id}/status` has nothing to stream until the build finishes. Insert the row with `status=RUNNING` at the top of both `full_build` and `patch_build`, carry `run_id` through, flip to `SUCCESS`/`ERROR` at the end instead of inserting a new row
- Repo cache eviction: TTL (7d idle) + LRU disk-budget; mark `repo_clones.evicted_at`, keep row as tombstone for re-clone

## API surface
- `GET /trees/{tree_id}` — no trees route exists yet
- `WS /repos/{graph_id}/status` — stream build progress; depends on the RUNNING row being open first (see above)
- Widen FastAPI exception handling — `api/routes/repos.py` only catches `CloneError` and `ValueError`; parse, Leiden, and DB errors propagate as raw 500s

## Frontend (C7)
- WebSocket build progress in RepoDashboard — connect to `WS /repos/{graph_id}/status` and drive the stage list from server events rather than a 3 s poll + elapsed-time heuristic
- Semantic zoom — community super-nodes at low zoom, god nodes + boundaries at mid, all labelled nodes at high zoom

## Skill file / agent context (new)
- `GET /repos/{graph_id}/context?q=<keywords>` — new C1 endpoint; runs the C6 BFS subgraph logic but returns a formatted plain-text context block instead of an LLM answer; used by skill files and the MCP server
- Skill file generator — `GET /repos/{graph_id}/skill-file?tool=<claude|cursor|copilot|windsurf>` returns a tool-specific markdown file as a download (`Content-Disposition: attachment`); bakes `graph_id` + Meridian base URL into the file at generation time; long-lived read-only graph token bundled so the file is self-contained
- Tool-specific templates (one per target):
  - Claude Code → `.claude/commands/hds-context.md` (bash + curl block, `$ARGUMENTS` interpolation)
  - Cursor → `.cursor/rules/hds-context.mdc` (Cursor Rules frontmatter + inline instruction)
  - GitHub Copilot → `.github/copilot-instructions.md` (plain markdown, injected into every prompt)
  - Windsurf → `.windsurfrules` (plain markdown)
- Long-lived read-only graph token — scoped to a single `graph_id`, read-only, non-expiring; issued at skill-file download time so the file works without the user managing JWT rotation
- MCP server (`/mcp` endpoint, SSE transport) — exposes two tools: `get_context(keywords, depth=2)` and `get_community(community_id)`; works with Claude Code, Cursor, Windsurf, Cline, Continue — any MCP-capable tool; this is the long-term universal interface, skill files are the short-term bridge
- Frontend download button — "Download for your AI tool" dropdown on the graph detail page; calls the skill-file generator endpoint; no install required on the user's side

## Auth cleanup
- Drop `_SYSTEM_USER_ID` placeholder in `graph_engine/utils/db_utils.py` — `sync_repo` now receives a real `user_id` from the JWT (wired through `api/routes/repos.py → orchestrator → full_build/patch_build`); the system-user fixture and its ensure-system-user bootstrap can be removed
- Flip `trees.graph_id` (`nullable=True` in `db/entities/tree.py:31`) and `repo_clones.user_id` (`nullable=True` in `db/entities/repo_clone.py:28`) to `NOT NULL` once every code path is user-scoped (blocked by the `_SYSTEM_USER_ID` removal above)

